  "worked_solution": "Here the limits of the numerator and denominator are ${lim}_{x\\to {\\frac{\\pi }{2}}^{-}}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x)=-\\infty $ and ${lim}_{x\\to {\\frac{\\pi }{2}}^{-}}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x)=\\infty ,$ respectively, so we have the case $\\frac{-\\infty }{\\infty }.$\n\nApplying L'Hopital's rule, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {\\frac{\\pi }{2}}^{-}}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x)}{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x)} & ={lim}_{x\\to {\\frac{\\pi }{2}}^{-}}\\frac{[\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x)]^{\u2032}}{{[\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x)]}^{\u2032}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {\\frac{\\pi }{2}}^{-}}\\frac{(-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x})}{(\\frac{{sec}^{2}\u2061x}{\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x})} \\\\  & =-{lim}_{x\\to {\\frac{\\pi }{2}}^{-}}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x}{{sec}^{2}\u2061x\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x} \\\\  & =-{lim}_{x\\to {\\frac{\\pi }{2}}^{-}}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x})}{(\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}\u2061x})\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x} \\\\  & =-{lim}_{x\\to {\\frac{\\pi }{2}}^{-}}\\frac{{sin}^{2}\u2061x}{(\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}\u2061x}){cos}^{2}\u2061x} \\\\  & =-{lim}_{x\\to {\\frac{\\pi }{2}}^{-}}{sin}^{2}\u2061x \\\\  & =-{sin}^{2}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
